    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a condensed active roster, as our core heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are sidelined by a team-wide off-day. Consequently, **Drake Baldwin** emerges as our primary offensive engine. With a score of 57.79, **Drake Baldwin** is the only player approaching the \"Strong\" threshold today, bolstered significantly by his placement in the leadoff spot against Aaron Nola. While Nola\u2019s 3.93 xERA poses a legitimate challenge, the 10% efficiency bump for batting first keeps **Drake Baldwin** as an essential start to maximize our limited opportunities in the Runs category.\n\nOur secondary slot is occupied by **Dominic Smith**, who rounds out the lineup with a score of 44.87. While **Dominic Smith** sits in the \"Marginal\" category, his platoon advantage against the right-handed Nola provides enough leverage to justify the start over our other prospects. The optimizer looked closely at the depth chart, weighing whether to deploy players like **Jackson Merrill** or **Andy Pages** if they were available, but the current scheduling void across the league left us with little flexibility. Meanwhile, **Luis Robert Jr.** remains firmly on the bench due to his IL designation, and we continue to monitor the development paths of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Henry Bolte**.\n\nThe primary risk today is the matchup against a high-caliber pitcher in Nola, whose ability to limit baserunners creates a suppressed ceiling for both **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith**. Given that we are hunting for scarcity-driven production, the lack of sprint-speed specialists in today's lineup\u2014specifically the absence of **Nasim Nunez** or **Wade Meckler** in favorable spots\u2014means our SB output is effectively neutralized for this cycle. We will prioritize efficiency and volume from our two active starters, effectively treating today as a preservation day while we await the return of our full core from the league-wide scheduling lull.",
